      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it feels like you're mostly just giving the standard debunking stuff. like, if scientists are actually finding these correlations in the data, isn't it a bit biased to just call them \"flawed\" without explaining why the data is actually considered reliable by some? what are the actual specific evidence points they use to argue that these differences aren't just environmental?",
