      "content": "Some proponents of the idea argue that genetic differences are driving IQ disparities across racial groups due to adaptations for specific environments. For example, they cite studies suggesting that Africans and others of African descent have a genetic adaptation that may have favored physical strength advantages in their ancestors under struggled environments, but not necessarily in test-taking situations that do not favor such interventions, whereas East Asians have been positively selected for in environments where high education is valued.",
